# Mutation cases for §scxml-5.7.1 — what a `<param>` whose expression will
# not evaluate costs the message it was travelling on.
#
# Run with `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/send_param_error_is_reported_ctest.cases`.
#
# The clause has two halves: "MUST place the error 'error.execution' on the
# internal event queue" AND "MUST ignore the name and value". Measured
# 2026-08-21, five of the seven channels kept neither, each in its own way —
# C++ (both engines), Kotlin and C11 logged nothing a document could read and
# then wrote a placeholder under the param's name; Python reported the error
# and discarded the entire message. Rust and Go were already right, which is
# why they are the shape the rest were brought to.
#
# The message is not discarded. §scxml-6.2.3's "discard the message" is about
# `<send>`'s own arguments, and reading it over a `<param>` leaves "ignore the
# name and value" with nothing to mean. W3C test343 settles it from the other
# side of the same clause: an illegal `<param>` under `<donedata>` raises
# `error.execution` and the `done.state` event still arrives, with empty data.
# `DoneDataHelper::evaluateParams` had that reading written down all along.
#
# The C11 target is the TEMPLATE rather than a generated file, for the reason
# `c11_datamodel_reader.cases` gives: this backend commits no generated tree,
# so the template is what the built binaries carry. The C++ AOT target is a
# template for the same reason its output is a build product — `--write-deps`
# makes the generated header depend on every jinja2 file that rendered it, so
# an edit here reaches the binary the round runs.
#
# The Kotlin, Go and Python halves of this axis have no round: the harness
# reaches cargo and ctest only (open debt M8/N10). Their witness is the same
# fixture run in their own suites.
#
# Anchors are literal slices of the source; an edit that moves one is
# reported INCONCLUSIVE with the anchor quoted, never as a pass.

mutation_ctest --test-dir build -R '^(IntegrationTests|c11_integration_send_param_payload)$'
mutation_targets sce/src/runtime/ActionExecutorImpl.cpp tools/codegen/templates/actions/send.jinja2 tools/codegen/templates/c/state_machine.c.jinja2
mutation_oracles tests/integration/SendParamPayloadTest.cpp tests/integration/SendParamPayloadAotTest.cpp backends/c/tests/integration/test_send_param_payload.c

# ── C++ Interpreter: the report ────────────────────────────────────
#
# Dropping the pair without saying so. The payload still arrives intact
# minus the failed name, so only `failNoParamError` can see it — which is
# the point: correctness of the payload was never the half that was missing.

mutation_case "the cpp interpreter drops the failed param without reporting it" <<'PY'
edit("sce/src/runtime/ActionExecutorImpl.cpp",
     """                        if (eventRaiser_) {
                            eventRaiser_->raiseEvent("error.execution", "<send> <param name='" + param.name +
                                                                            "'> expr failed to evaluate");
                        }
                        aParamFailed = true;
                        continue;""",
     """                        aParamFailed = true;
                        continue;""")
PY

# ── C++ Interpreter: ignoring the name ─────────────────────────────
#
# The shipped behaviour before this axis: the failed reading goes out under
# the param's name. `error.execution` is still raised, so `failNoParamError`
# stays quiet and `failBrokenParamDelivered` is the only witness.

mutation_case "the cpp interpreter carries the failed param under its name" <<'PY'
edit("sce/src/runtime/ActionExecutorImpl.cpp",
     """                        continue;
                    }
                    std::string paramValue =""",
     """                        evaluatedParams[param.name].push_back("");
                        continue;
                    }
                    std::string paramValue =""")
PY

# ── C++ AOT: the report ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# One macro serves all five arms of the send template, so removing the raise
# here removes it from every `<send>` shape the backend emits.

mutation_case "the cpp aot template logs the failed param instead of reporting it" <<'PY'
edit("tools/codegen/templates/actions/send.jinja2",
     """{{ indent }}engine.raise(typename Engine::EventWithMetadata(
{{ indent }}    Event::Error_execution,
{{ indent }}    "<send> <param name='{{ param.name | escape_cpp }}'> could not be read"));""",
     """{{ indent }}(void)0;""")
PY

# ── C++ AOT: ignoring the name ─────────────────────────────────────

# Injected at ONE call site rather than into `param_eval_failed`. The macro is
# shared by six arms and they do not agree on what the container is called —
# four have `params`, one has `hostRequest.params`, one has `httpParams` — so a
# `params[...]` in the macro body is `'params' was not declared in this scope`
# on the last two, and the whole tree stops compiling. That was INCONCLUSIVE,
# which is a case that cannot run rather than a case that found nothing.
#
# The site below is the immediate-send arm, which is the one the fixture's
# `<send target="#_internal" event="withBadParam">` is generated through
# (confirmed against `send_param_payload_sm.inl`, whose failure branch sits
# under a locally declared `params`). Its `param_eval_failed` call is the only
# one indented eight, which is what makes the anchor unique.
mutation_case "the cpp aot template carries the failed param under its name" <<'PY'
edit("tools/codegen/templates/actions/send.jinja2",
     """    } else {
{{ param_eval_failed(param, '        ') }}
    }""",
     """    } else {
{{ param_eval_failed(param, '        ') }}
        params["{{ param.name | escape_cpp }}"].push_back("");
    }""")
PY

# ⚠ Re-aimed 2026-09-27: C11 no longer assembles the payload as Lua source in
# a C buffer. `send_payload_json` gathers each pair in Lua with one
# `table.insert` that either happens whole or not at all, and serialises the
# list once. The half-written-pair rewind and the separator decision these
# cases used to break no longer exist to break; the two below are the defects
# the gatherer can have instead.

# ── C11: the report ────────────────────────────────────────────────

mutation_case "the c11 template drops the failed param without reporting it" <<'PY'
edit("tools/codegen/templates/c/state_machine.c.jinja2",
     """                    {{ csym_prefix }}{{ machine }}_raise_platform_error(
                        sm, {{ csym_prefix | upper }}{{ machine | upper }}_EVENT_ERROR_EXECUTION,
                        "<send> <param name='{{ param.name | escape_c }}'> expr failed to evaluate");""",
     """                    (void)sm;""")
PY

# ── C11: ignoring the name ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The shipped behaviour before this axis: the failed reading goes out under
# the param's name. `error.execution` is still raised, so `failNoParamError`
# stays quiet and `failBrokenParamDelivered` is the only witness.

mutation_case "the c11 template carries the failed param under its name" <<'PY'
edit("tools/codegen/templates/c/state_machine.c.jinja2",
     """                        "<send> <param name='{{ param.name | escape_c }}'> expr failed to evaluate");
                    _param_failed = true;""",
     """                        "<send> <param name='{{ param.name | escape_c }}'> expr failed to evaluate");
                    (void)luaL_dostring(sm->L,
                        "table.insert(_sce_send_pairs, {\\"{{ param.name | escape_lua | escape_c }}\\", ''})");
                    _param_failed = true;""")
PY

# ── C11: the send's own pairs ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# Each send starts a fresh pair list, and the serialiser clears it. Without
# the start, the first `table.insert` of every send reaches a list that is
# not there, so every param of every send fails: `error.execution` for each,
# and payloads that arrive empty — `failSiblingParamLost`, and the typed
# phase before it.

mutation_case "the c11 template gathers without starting the send's pair list" <<'PY'
edit("tools/codegen/templates/c/state_machine.c.jinja2",
     """                (void)luaL_dostring(sm->L, "_sce_send_pairs = {}");""",
     """                (void)0;""")
PY
